# Vault .gitignore (seeded by /brain:init).
# Marker comment lines (the ones below naming why an entry is required) are
# the plugin's dependency set — /brain:doctor check 9 (bin/check-gitignore.sh)
# parses THIS file for them, so the template stays the one definition. Keep
# each marker on its own line directly above its entry.
# Harvested transcripts are private staging — never commit them (POC §14.7).
# doctor:required private harvest staging — must never be committed (POC §14.7)
chats/

# graphify machine-specific scratch (interpreter path, detect/extract temp, cost log).
# The durable artifacts (graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md, manifest.json) ARE committed.
# doctor:required graphify scratch under graphify-out/ — machine-specific, never shared
graphify-out/.graphify_*
# doctor:required graphify scratch anywhere in the tree — machine-specific, never shared
**/.graphify_*
# doctor:required graphify root pin — POSIX-vs-native path is per-checkout
.graphify_root
# doctor:required graphify interpreter cache — per-machine, goes stale when moved
.graphify_python

# Machine-local state about in-flight brain commands: the wiki/hot.md pin that
# bin/write-hot.sh compares against, and the session record bin/session.sh writes
# (--start / --status / --end). Per-checkout and per-session — never shared, and
# deliberately NOT in .saveinclude, so no command can commit it. A git worktree
# gets its own .brain/, which is what makes parallel sessions genuinely isolated.
# doctor:required machine-local session state (hot.md pin, session record) — never shared
.brain/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.obsidian/workspace*
node_modules/
